-- title:
--   Cyclic Γ(q)-action of order dividing q+1 on the blow-up chart
-- statement:
--   **Numerical and field data.** Fix primes $q$ and $\ell$ with $5\le q$, $3\le\ell$ and $\ell\ne q$, and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$ and $\ell\nmid M'$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic $0$ and $\xi\in L$ a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity; the hypothesis `hι` asks for a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq \operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$, and let `hK` identify $K$ with [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH (q*ℓ) M'))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), that is, the subfield of $L((t))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image (under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81)) of the $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb Q$ of level $\Gamma_H$, where $N_0=(q\ell)^2M'$ and $H=$ `levelH (q*ℓ) M'` is the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/N_0)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times$, i.e. the subgroup of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   **Base ring and chart algebra.** Let $A$ be a henselian local discrete valuation domain with an algebra structure over $L$ making $L$ its fraction field and with algebraically closed residue field, such that $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and $\xi$ lies in the image of $A$ in $L$ (`hξA`); $A$ acts on $K$ compatibly with $L$ (scalar tower). Let $j$ be a nonzero element of $K$ whose Laurent series is the image under [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157), the $q$-expansion $t^{-1}+\dots$ of the modular invariant. Let $\varpi\in A$ with $\mathfrak m_A=(\varpi)$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t\in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`). Write $C=$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j]$.
--
--   **Supersingular maximal ideal.** Let $y\subset C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing the image of $\varpi$ (`hϖy`), and supersingular in the following sense (`hss`): for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no nonzero point annihilated by $q$.
--
--   **Level automorphisms.** For $\gamma\in SL(2,\mathbb Z)$ and an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$, the predicate [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L (q*ℓ) ξ (q*ℓ) ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M') γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29) asserts: for every weight $k$, every pair $f,g$ of modular forms of weight $k$ for $\Gamma_H(N_0)$ (viewed inside $GL(2,\mathbb R)$) with integral $q$-expansions represented by power series $p_f,p_g$ over $\mathbb Z$, $p_g$ having nonzero Laurent series, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficient extension of $p_f/p_g$, and every embedding $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, the coefficientwise image under $\iota$ of the Laurent series of $\tau x$, multiplied by the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$, equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k \mathrm{conjElemN}(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$, where $\mathrm{conjElemN}(m)\,\delta=\begin{pmatrix}\delta_{00}&\delta_{01}/m\\ m\,\delta_{10}&\delta_{11}\end{pmatrix}$.
--
--   **The chart hypothesis `hArig`.** Let $\mathfrak X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two affine charts $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin` and $\operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf` over the middle chart, with its structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and the morphism `ιFin` from $\operatorname{Spec} C$. The hypothesis `hArig` requires, for every point $z$ of $\mathfrak X$ at which the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk, and every point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ with `ιFin` $y'=z$ whose prime $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ satisfies the same supersingularity condition as above (`hss'`), the existence of a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f-\bigl(X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1\bigr)\in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the Drinfeld form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of the stalk $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ onto $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v-fu\bigr)$, subject to seven clauses, summarised here: ($\alpha$) $e$ carries the image of $a\in A$ to the class of the constant $C(\sigma a)$; ($\beta$) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserves $C$; ($\gamma$) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma(\ell)$ such a $\tau$ acts trivially on $C$ modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$; ($\delta$) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and acting trivially modulo $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, an element $c\in W$ and a matrix $M\in M_2(W)$ such that $\theta$ intertwines the action of $\tau$ on germs through $e$, fixes all constants, satisfies $\theta(X_{j})\equiv\sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the classes of $X_0,X_1$, with $c^{q+1}\equiv 1$ and $M_{ij}\equiv c\,\gamma_{ij}$ modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, with $c\equiv 1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, and with $c\not\equiv1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; ($\varepsilon$) a branch-separation clause: two primes of $S$ lying over $\sigma\varpi$, not containing both classes of $X_0,X_1$, and containing elements $a_iX_0+b_iX_1+h_i$ with $h_i\in(X_0,X_1)^2$ and $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions to the stalk along $e$; ($\zeta$) for a prime $P$ of $S$ lying over $\sigma\varpi$, not containing both classes of $X_0,X_1$ and containing an element $X_0+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a\in C$ has germ in the contraction of $P$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; ($\eta$) a leading-form clause for [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) (the series obtained from the $q$-expansion of $j$ by multiplying all exponents by $q\ell$): it lies in $K$ and in $C$, and for a suitable $a_0\in A$ with difference in $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}$ there are $e_0\ge1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ form is a unit at every pair $(a,b)\in W^2$ with $a$ or $b$ a unit and $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_W$, such that $e$ sends the germ of that difference to the class of $h$.
--
--   **Pinned point and pinned chart witness.** Next, a particular such point is fixed: $z$ in $\mathfrak X$, the germ $\varpi_z$ of $\varpi$, lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$, a point $y'$ of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ over $z$ satisfying `hss'`, and `hy'y`: $y'.\mathrm{asIdeal}=y$. Further, one chart witness at $z$ is fixed: a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, $\sigma_1:A\to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$, $f_1,u_1,v_1$ with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and an isomorphism $e_1$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal O_{\mathfrak X,z}$ onto $S=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1\bigr)$; the hypothesis `hW₁` asserts for this witness the same seven clauses ($\alpha$)–($\eta$) just listed.
--
--   **The centre $J$, the algebra $B$ and the valuation subring $W$.** The ideal $J\subset C$ is pinned by `hJ` to be the infimum of the set of ideals of the form $\mathrm{comap}_{\tau|_C}\bigl(\mathrm{comap}_{e_1\circ\mathrm{germ}_z}\,(\sigma_1\varpi_t,X_0,X_1)S\bigr)$, taken over all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$. The subalgebra $B\subseteq K$ is pinned by `hB` to be the $A$-subalgebra underlying the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x\in K:\ x\varpi_t\in J\}$, i.e. $B=C[J/\varpi_t]$. Let $W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ with $B\subseteq W$ (`hBW`).
--
--   Four further hypothesis blocks are imposed. `hR1` (two clauses): $C\subseteq B$, and every element of $K$ is a quotient $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\ne0$. `hR2` (three clauses): $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation, and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$. `hR3` (five clauses): an element of $L$ lies in $W$ exactly when it comes from $A$; $\mathfrak m_W$ is generated by the image of $\varpi$; $W$ is a discrete valuation ring; an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathfrak m_W$; and $W$ is the set of quotients $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and $h\notin\mathfrak m_W$. `hEQ` (five clauses): first, for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho$ from $B$ onto the Drinfeld coordinate ring [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q (ResidueField A)`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) $=\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)[X_0,X_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly}-1)$ whose kernel is $B\cap\mathfrak m_W$, which is compatible with $A\to\mathrm{ResidueField}(A)$, and which is equivariant in the following sense: for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $W$, there is a unit $c$ of $\mathbb F_{q^2}$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of $(g,c)\mapsto \det(g)\,c^{q+1}$) such that $\rho\circ\tau=\mathrm{hAction}(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)\circ\rho$ on $B$, and $c\ne1$ whenever $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; second, $B$ is stable under every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; third, every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is the image, under some level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, of $B\cap\mathfrak m_W$; fourth, an element of $B$ all of whose translates under such automorphisms lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$ in $B$; fifth, a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserves $W$ as soon as it preserves $y$ on $C$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses there exist a natural number $n$ with $1\le n$ and $n\mid q+1$, an element $\gamma_0\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$, and a level automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K$ at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ (in the sense of `IsLevelAutAt` above) satisfying $f\in W\iff\tau_0f\in W$ for all $f\in K$, such that:
--
--   1. $\tau_0^{\,n}$ fixes $B$ pointwise: $(\tau_0^{\,n})f=f$ for every $f\in B$;
--
--   2. no smaller positive power does so: for every $k$ with $0<k<n$ there is $f\in B$ with $(\tau_0^{\,k})f\ne f$;
--
--   3. every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $W$ (i.e. $f\in W\iff\tau f\in W$) agrees on $B$ with a power of $\tau_0$: there is $k<n$ with $\tau f=(\tau_0^{\,k})f$ for all $f\in B$.
--
--   Thus the automorphisms of $K$ of $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$-level type which fix the valuation $W$ act on $B$ through a cyclic group of order $n$ dividing $q+1$, generated by the restriction of $\tau_0$.
--
--   This is the cyclicity step in the analysis of the ends of the blown-up supersingular chart: at a supersingular point of the integral model of the modular curve of level $\Gamma_H((q\ell)^2M')$, the part of the decomposition group coming from $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and fixing the exceptional valuation is shown to act on the blow-up algebra $B=C[J/\varpi_t]$ through a cyclic group whose order divides $q+1$, the order of the relevant torus in the Drinfeld fibre. It feeds the assembly statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_cyclicDecomposition_ends_moduliHasse_igusaSepTranslate_commonChart_cover_blowupChart_linked_of_eq_adjoin_of_drinfeldChartWitness`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_cyclicDecomposition_ends_moduliHasse_igusaSepTranslate_commonChart_cover_blowupChart_linked_of_eq_adjoin_of_drinfeldChartWitness), and uses the uniqueness, multiplicativity and triviality properties of level automorphisms recorded in [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.isLevelAutAt_unique_mul_one_of_exists_ringHom`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.isLevelAutAt_unique_mul_one_of_exists_ringHom).
